# mpd-defaults.env — the default value of every mdl-demo setting.
#
# Read this file to answer "what happens if I set nothing?" for an
# mdl-demo project.
#
# Do not edit it. It ships with mpd and an update overwrites it. To change a
# value, override it in a project's own /srv/projects/<name>/mpd.env (a type
# default like this one wins over an ambient value from your vm.env).


# Database
#
# An mdl-demo project is the source tree of the mdl-demo tool. mpd runs no
# server and no database for it, so this is empty.
#
# Keep it empty. The value is doing work: an empty setting here overrides
# any MPD_DB you set for all your projects in
# /var/lib/mpd/env/vm.env, which would otherwise give this project a
# database it never uses.
MPD_DB=""
